---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { absolute, site, url } from '../lib/site';

const description =
  'Lina is an editor’s list of hotels that look like a splurge. It is operated by Nadav Stern. A price or a Booking.com score is printed only after it has been read on the listing.';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'AboutPage',
  name: 'About Lina',
  url: absolute('/about'),
  description,
  mainEntity: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: site.name,
    email: site.email,
    url: absolute('/'),
  },
};
---

<Base title="About" description={description} section="about" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article class="wrap page-hero">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'About' }]} />
    <p class="kicker">The edit</p>
    <h1>A list with a budget, and a rule about numbers.</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Lina looks for hotels that feel like a treat and often land around $80 to $150 a night, plus the occasional
        place that is honestly expensive. The audience is international. The cities on the desk right now are
        <a href={url('/cities/paris')}>Paris</a>, <a href={url('/cities/rome')}>Rome</a>, and
        <a href={url('/cities/barcelona')}>Barcelona</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The rule is stricter than the taste. A nightly rate is published only after it has been checked for a date, a
        room, and an occupancy. A Booking.com score is printed only with the review count and the day it was read.
        If a figure has not been checked, the record stays marked TODO and the button sends you to Booking.com. The
        rates on the site now were read on 23 October 2026 for the night of 10–11 November, two adults.
      </p>
      <p>
        Hotel pages do not use another building’s photograph and call it the property. City pages use royalty-free
        photographs from Unsplash, with the photographer credited on the picture.
      </p>
      <h2>Who runs it</h2>
      <p>
        Lina is operated by {site.operator}. The earlier version of this site was a Hebrew page of checked lodging
        deals in Israel. This English edition replaces it. The repository name is unchanged.
      </p>
      <p>
        Questions, corrections, and hotels worth a look go to
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, or through the <a href={url('/contact')}>contact page</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some links earn a commission if you book. That is explained in the
        <a href={url('/disclosure')}>affiliate disclosure</a>, and in a short line next to the booking buttons.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
